## Context

`c2c install grok` ships CLI-first: skill + SessionStart/SessionEnd hooks + no MCP by default.
Preferred inbound is Monitor + `c2c monitor`. Plugin packaging was explicitly deferred.

## Desired later

A Grok plugin (`~/.grok/plugins/c2c` or marketplace) that bundles:
- assembled grok /c2c skill
- SessionStart/SessionEnd hooks (`c2c hook grok`)
- optional slash command `/c2c`
- optional MCP entry (opt-in only; not default)

## Why defer

CLI + global hooks + skill already cover vanilla Grok without trust/marketplace friction.
Plugin is packaging polish + one-step trust model, not delivery quality.

## Depends on

Landed (or landing): skill snippet assembly, `c2c install grok`, `c2c hook grok`, GROK_SESSION_ID.

## Acceptance (when picked up)

- `grok plugin install <c2c-plugin> --trust` enables same surfaces as `c2c install grok`
- `c2c uninstall grok` / plugin uninstall leaves no owned files
- No MCP by default unless opt-in flag